## Quick-reference constants

- z_{0,1} = 2.4048255577 (fundamental drum mode)
- K_drum(15 cm, c=100 m/s) = 106.103 Hz; f_{0,1} = 255.1 Hz
- Square K' = c/(2L); steel plate L=0.30 m, membrane-model c=1500 m/s → K' = 2500 Hz; f_{1,1} = K'√2 ≈ 3536 Hz (illustrative; a real 30 cm steel plate's actual flexural fundamental is far lower — plate option mandatory for metal)
- Flexural plate coefficient for steel: √(E/(12ρ(1−ν²))) ≈ √(210e9/(12·7850·0.91)) ≈ 1567 (SI), f_{p,q} ≈ 1567·(h/L²)·(p²+q²); h=1 mm, L=0.30 m → K'' ≈ 17.4 Hz, f_{1,1} ≈ 35 Hz (order-of-magnitude; free-edge corrections O(1)).
